WEBVTT

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Hi, Zach. I'm Whitney.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:13.000
zack9: Hi, Whitney. Nice to meet you.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Nice to meet you. How's your day going?

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.000
zack9: Uh, pretty good, how about you?

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:35.000
Whitney Hodges: Good, thanks. Well, thanks so much for scheduling a call and for applying for the ads accelerators. I'm looking forward to learning more about your business and what you've been doing with ads and just kind of exploring to see if the accelerators would be a good fit for you.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Obviously, answer any questions that you might have.

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:39.000
zack9: Okay. Yeah.

00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Whitney Hodges: So, it sounds like you've been doing quite a bit with ads already on both the Meta and the Google Ads side. I'd love for you to kind of tell me a little bit more about that. Have you been running the ads yourself?

00:01:52.000 --> 00:02:04.000
zack9: Uh, yeah, I've been running the ads myself. I actually paid for a different course, um… about, I don't know, probably about a year ago now. Um… and I've seen okay results, uh…

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:16.000
zack9: honestly, on the… the Google Ads, I've been running a little bit longer, because it seemed to me to be a little bit more straightforward, and most of what I've done is just, like, uh… has been on our… because I own a flower shop.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:22.000
zack9: My wife's really the one… I just do the marketing and stuff for her. She's the one who does all the actual work.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.000
Whitney Hodges: Yes.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:31.000
zack9: So, I just helped with the marketing, and uh… so on the Google Ads side, we… I've only used it for, like, everyday stuff. I haven't done… done it for, like, the wedding florals. Um…

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:34.000
zack9: And that's gone well, um…

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:49.000
zack9: Overall, I would say, we're spending probably about, like, $2,000 a month, and I haven't been able to really get the spend above that, um, and about the max I could get it without it kind of falling off in terms of, like, our…

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:54.000
zack9: Um, cost to acquire a customer just goes way up. Um…

00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:54.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:03:03.000
zack9: And that's mostly because I think that targets, like, the cities that we're in. If I try and move to, like, adjacent cities that we deliver to, it just falls off.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:02:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.000
zack9: Okay, Fred is pretty normal, a little bit harder to do, maybe I just don't.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.000
zack9: I'm not good enough at it, um…

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:15.000
zack9: to feel comfortable doing that. Uh, so we're about $2,000 a month for the Google Ads, um…

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:16.000
Whitney Hodges: No.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:24.000
zack9: Then, uh, the meta ads, we only started about a year ago, and that's been strictly for the weddings we're running that for.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:24.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.000
zack9: And I'm up to about…

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:30.000
zack9: Uh, I think I'm almost to $100 a day right now.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:32.000
Whitney Hodges: Wow, uh-huh.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:44.000
zack9: almost $3,000 a month, um, and I'm having a little bit of trouble with, uh, attribution, I think, partially, and then I'm also having a little bit of trouble with.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:42.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:47.000
zack9: Like, cause our direct, um…

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:49.000
zack9: like…

00:03:49.000 --> 00:04:07.000
zack9: gross profit to cost to acquire is only, like, 2 to 1, which seems really low to me for the funnel and the amount of work it is. I mean, we're obviously getting, like, a lot more, like, website inquiries and stuff, and I've noticed if I, like, scale down the spin, those definitely go down, so I know there's definitely… we're catching more people that way, too.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:12.000
zack9: Whether they're being attributed correctly or not. You know what I mean?

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:16.000
zack9: And I don't know, I just feel like we're kind of at…

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:22.000
zack9: from what I've looked at, we're a little bit low, like, on our close rate, and we're a little bit low, I think, on our, um…

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:29.000
zack9: People that book, uh, from Leeds, and we're not… we're not super dialed on, like.

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:33.000
zack9: Super fast speed to lead response, um…

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:36.000
zack9: So I'm sure that's part of it, too, but…

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:44.000
zack9: Um, yeah, so I don't know, I'm… the people that I've been doing it with, I've had okay results with, I'm just not sure…

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Thank you.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:48.000
zack9: some of the questions I'm asking now, I feel like they're not really giving me, like, good answers to, so…

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.000
Whitney Hodges: Got it.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:50.000
zack9: Not loving it. Yeah.

00:04:50.000 --> 00:05:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, makes sense. Okay, so lots of good stuff going on here, but lots to unpack as well, and sounds like a good amount of opportunity also. So, I think maybe tell me a little bit more about the courses or programs that you're currently in. Is it something to help you with both Google and Meta collectively, or is it…

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:15.000
zack9: No, it's just the meta, just the meta stuff. That's more of what I've been trying to work on, because I…

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Different stuff for each of those.

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:16.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:18.000
zack9: I mean, I'm in Northern California, so…

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:26.000
zack9: I mean, there's tons of people local to me for weddings. We have a bigger delivery area for weddings, definitely. Um, so, like…

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.000
zack9: I don't feel like… I don't know, I feel like.

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:35.000
zack9: I need to work on one before I worry about the other one, I guess. Um, and I think with the Google Ads, too.

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:05:35.000 --> 00:05:46.000
zack9: uh, our website's kind of been part of the handicap there. Um, we inherited it from the people we bought the business from, and I don't love it. It's, uh, pretty shitty. But we haven't switched it yet, and…

00:05:38.000 --> 00:05:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:54.000
zack9: With the Meta ads, we're just running, uh, the lead form or whatever through Meta, so it's not going to a landing page or anything like that.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.000
Whitney Hodges: Uh-huh.

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Uh-huh.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.000
zack9: So, that…

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:04.000
zack9: I guess the website's been kind of a handicap for the Google Ads, I feel like, somewhat.

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, yeah.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.000
zack9: Because it's not… it's, like, old, and it's… the company that we use is pretty…

00:06:11.000 --> 00:06:13.000
zack9: I don't know, antiquated, I think.

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:13.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:19.000
zack9: Um, and hard for me to make adjustments, and they're not very good about making adjustments that I want.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:25.000
zack9: You know what I mean? So it kind of makes it hard to go to, like, landing pages and be more dynamic with that for the Google ad, I feel like.

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:26.000
Whitney Hodges: Right.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, no, that all totally makes sense. And so I saw that you're using GHL. Is the website built in GHL, or is the website somewhere different?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:39.000
zack9: No, the website's somewhere different, um…

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:48.000
zack9: Yeah, it's hosted through a different company that we started with our everyday florals, and there was a wedding page on there. The old owner of the flower shop didn't really, like.

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:55.000
zack9: try to do weddings, you know what I mean? Just the ones she got through referral and stuff like that, that wasn't really the main part of her business.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:56.000
zack9: Oh.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:02.000
zack9: So yeah, it's been something where we've been trying to actively grow, it just seems like it's higher margin, and.

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:11.000
zack9: And my wife and her team like doing the weddings, so we've been trying to grow those more. It's really what I've been focused on the last year or so.

00:07:06.000 --> 00:07:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:10.000
Whitney Hodges: No.

00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:26.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm, okay, amazing, love that, yeah. And definitely hear what you're saying, you know, about the website, you know, it probably, um, you know, could be time for, you know, a branding refresh, you know, a new website on a new platform sort of thing, um, but…

00:07:26.000 --> 00:07:43.000
Whitney Hodges: So you're aware in GHL, you do have the ability to build landing pages there, right? So that actually is the route that we recommend for Meta Ads and both Google Ads, honestly, is building a dedicated.

00:07:43.000 --> 00:08:02.000
Whitney Hodges: landing page specifically for ads traffic. And we find that on the meta ad side, that that can produce higher quality leads than just having somebody fill out the lead form. So, um, so that's definitely, you know, an area of opportunity there as well.

00:08:05.000 --> 00:08:06.000
zack9: Okay.

00:08:06.000 --> 00:08:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Now, on the Google Ads side, I know you said you've really just kind of been focusing there on the daily orders, things like that, um, but it sounds like, you know, future state, you would probably be interested in maybe, like, running some wedding-specific.

00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.000
Whitney Hodges: campaigns for Google Ads, you just haven't tried that yet, is that right?

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.000
zack9: Yeah, I'm not…

00:08:24.000 --> 00:08:30.000
zack9: I'm not against it. I tried it once, like, towards the beginning, and then, um…

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:37.000
zack9: it didn't work out that well, and our website sucked, and I was trying to make changes, and it was tough for me to make changes on the website, and I just kind of…

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:38.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:50.000
zack9: dropped it at that point. I think I was working on other stuff, too, so it was something I tried a little bit, but I honestly didn't put a ton of effort into, and then I started working on the meta stuff, and then I was trying to just figure that out before I try and throw another thing in that I don't know how to.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:09:05.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. No, completely understand. And I totally get if you want to focus on the meta ad side of things first. Just kind of based on what we often see in terms of our clients' results is oftentimes when they are running on ads on two platforms.

00:09:05.000 --> 00:09:14.000
Whitney Hodges: simultaneously, right, Google and Meta, both for wedding campaigns, it will have a compounding effect in terms of the result.

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:17.000
zack9: I got you. So they'll maybe see you on Meta, and then they'll Google you, and they'll come through the ad, or.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:34.000
Whitney Hodges: And… and vice versa, right? Because somebody might Google you, um, you know, see you through your… your ad, right? And which, if you don't have, you know, amazing SEO authority with the website at this point, that could help you get found on Google more for weddings. At that point, they may not be ready to in…

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:40.000
Whitney Hodges: inquire immediately about the wedding, but through retargeting with the Meta Pixel, then they can see you through…

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.000
zack9: Yeah, I gotcha.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:43.000
Whitney Hodges: The meta ads. Mm-hmm.

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:58.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, so that would be kind of, um, you know, use case of kind of diving in and doing both, but also if you just wanted to focus on the meta ad side first, that is totally doable as well. Um…

00:09:58.000 --> 00:10:20.000
Whitney Hodges: And, you know, recommendations really that we would make there would be, you know, focusing first on an ads traffic landing page specifically for the meta ads. And as opposed to running those lead form campaigns, running conversion campaigns that would point to that ads traffic landing page to get people to.

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:26.000
Whitney Hodges: um, inquire, and then come through your… your GHL funnel.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:27.000
zack9: Gotcha, okay.

00:10:27.000 --> 00:10:37.000
Whitney Hodges: But you mentioned something about how you kind of felt like speed to lead was maybe, um, you know, kind of an area of opportunity for… for you guys, so…

00:10:36.000 --> 00:10:38.000
zack9: It definitely is.

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:38.000
Whitney Hodges: So fill me in on that.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:49.000
zack9: Uh, yeah, I mean, we're calling leads usually within 24 hours, that's all. I mean, sometimes we'll get to them much faster, um, but oftentimes not. That's why I say that that's been…

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.000
Whitney Hodges: Awesome.

00:10:45.000 --> 00:10:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:10:49.000 --> 00:10:52.000
zack9: Not great. I've been trying to be better about it, it just…

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. But through the GHL workflows, are they being… Oh, sorry, I think I lost you for a minute. But through the… Mm-hmm.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:11:01.000
zack9: They're getting automated, yeah, they're getting automated text and automated email immediately, and that gives them, um…

00:10:59.000 --> 00:11:00.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:11:01.000 --> 00:11:09.000
zack9: Some more info, like… because it seems like with florals, most brides don't really have, like, a great idea of what they even, like…

00:11:11.000 --> 00:11:22.000
zack9: Like, they will have, like, an idea of what they want, but they don't really know what it'll cost, or, like… because sometimes they'll have specific flowers that, you know, triple the cost of a wedding, you know, and so sometimes…

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.000
Whitney Hodges: Right. Mm-hmm.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:11:22.000 --> 00:11:34.000
zack9: They don't really even know that, so it's got a little bit of a guide to kind of give them a little more info, and then they also get a link that can book a call directly, because we get… in the lead form, we get, like, budget and… and the wedding date and stuff like that, so…

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:36.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm. Okay. Perfect.

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:41.000
zack9: But yeah, they get a link right away. So they do get an immediate text and an immediate email, they just don't get an immediate call.

00:11:40.000 --> 00:11:42.000
Whitney Hodges: That makes sense.

00:11:42.000 --> 00:11:44.000
zack9: Yeah.

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:59.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, I mean, right, it's going to take some time to get back in touch. After those initial touch points that are automated through GHL, are you continuing to nurture them with more email and text automations, or what does that look like?

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:59.000
zack9: Yeah, so, like…

00:11:59.000 --> 00:12:14.000
zack9: Yeah, so, I mean, it's a long… because some rides will be early, and florals kind of come towards… you kind of have to have, you know, like, your tables figured out, your venue figured out, so we're kind of one of the last vendors that you really want to go to. So I have, uh, it's like a 12…

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:09.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:12:14.000 --> 00:12:18.000
zack9: I think it might be 13-month automation that they're getting followed up with.

00:12:17.000 --> 00:12:20.000
Whitney Hodges: Wow. Okay, awesome. Mm-hmm.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:21.000
zack9: So it's pretty long.

00:12:20.000 --> 00:12:21.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:33.000
zack9: I mean, obviously, the first 7 days is a lot heavier, and then after that, it kind of falls off to, like, once a month, maybe, kind of checking in to see where they're at, or giving them some more info about, like, the things we do, um…

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:12:33.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:37.000
zack9: It's kind of how the workflow works.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:13:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah, that totally makes sense. It sounds like you have a really good foundation there, like the infrastructure, right? Like things are happening, leads are flowing in, they're being responded to, you're calling them within 24 hours. But typically what we see, you know, when sales still aren't ultimately where you want them to be or, you know, lead quality isn't necessarily where you want it to be, typically what it comes back to.

00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.000
zack9: Mm-hmm.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:13.000
Whitney Hodges: is an opportunity with messaging and positioning, and really strengthening that, right? And making sure that your unique value proposition comes across, right? That, um…

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:36.000
Whitney Hodges: ideal potential clients have a way to differentiate you from the the competitors, just kind of in terms of what they're seeing in your ad and your landing page. You know, throughout the email and text nurture sequences. Everything like that. So that's definitely a big area that the ads accelerators dig into as well as kind of like the foundations for success.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:52.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, with… with advertising, right? And how you can kind of do some, you know, like, self-reflection, you, like, and your wife, right? Of really kind of thinking about the types of weddings that you work on, what those clients are like, what the venues are like that you work at, what sets you guys apart.

00:13:52.000 --> 00:14:05.000
Whitney Hodges: So that all of that can be woven into the ad strategy, um, the landing page copy and design, you know, all the emails and everything that people are, um, receiving.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:22.000
Whitney Hodges: So, um, one other question I had, and was, you know, as far as the lead form ads that you're running, and I know you're spending, you know, a good amount every day, $100 a day, is it just… how many ads are you running, or how many campaigns are you running at this point, Zach?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
zack9: Um, well…

00:14:25.000 --> 00:14:36.000
zack9: uh… I guess there's two campaigns. There's a retargeting campaign, which I don't spend very much on, that… and that just takes the pixel from our website and, like, anyone that hits our Instagram or our Facebook page.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.000
Whitney Hodges: Nice.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.000
Whitney Hodges: None.

00:14:35.000 --> 00:14:37.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:41.000
zack9: Um, and retargets them. I think I'm gonna spend a dollar a day on that. It's pretty low, just to kind.

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:40.000
Whitney Hodges: Mm-hmm.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:46.000
zack9: For people that do hit our website or whatever, they kind of get hit a little bit more.

00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:43.000
Whitney Hodges: Sure.

00:14:44.000 --> 00:14:45.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:46.000
Whitney Hodges: Mmhm.

00:14:46.000 --> 00:14:49.000
zack9: For the actual, like, lead form, uh.

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:52.000
zack9: I only have one campaign, and it's got… I think I'm running, like…

00:14:52.000 --> 00:14:57.000
zack9: Two different ad sets, and each ad set, I think, has, like, 3 or 4 ads in it.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:07.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay, nice. Yeah, so you've got a good amount of variety in there. That's awesome. Um, love that. What's… so what is your cost per lead looking like, um, currently, Zach?

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
zack9: Yeah.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:07.000
zack9: Um… no.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:14.000
zack9: For, like, direct leads off of Meta, they're, like, 40 bucks each, I think, right now, is what they've been running.

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.000
Whitney Hodges: Yeah.

00:15:12.000 --> 00:15:34.000
Whitney Hodges: Okay. Okay. Mm-hmm. All right. Good to know. Yeah. I would say, you know, that that typically is the average that we're usually seeing across the board with leads coming in from Meta ads. But kind of as I described earlier, we're not usually going the lead form route, right? We're usually directing that traffic to a landing page and having them opt in from there.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:18.000
zack9: Yeah.

00:15:24.000 --> 00:15:25.000
zack9: Okay.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.000
zack9: Yeah.

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:47.000
Whitney Hodges: And that's… I mean, it's for a couple of different reasons, right? It's to help people… the right people self-qualify, and it's to help the wrong people self-disqualify, right? Because if they're only seeing an ad and then have a really simple form.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:16:09.000
Whitney Hodges: It's very easy. It's a very low barrier for them to opt in, which in terms of lead volume is great. But what we find works really well is to get them to that landing page so that they can learn more about the business, learn more about you, learn more about, you know, your wife and her team, the process, right? What, again, what kind of sets you guys apart?

00:16:09.000 --> 00:16:27.000
Whitney Hodges: you know, ensuring that pricing is visible, if they haven't already seen that, um, in an ad. And then you just kind of know from there, okay, this person's already kind of taken the time to consume more of our information and everything that's on this dedicated landing page, so in turn, you know, it ends up generating.

00:16:27.000 --> 00:16:46.000
Whitney Hodges: higher qualified leads, um, from our experience in terms of what we see. We also recommend kind of a full funnel approach with the meta ads, and we break this all down inside the ads accelerators as well. Um, typically, the majority of the budget is going into conversion campaigns, the way that you have it set up.

00:16:46.000 --> 00:17:01.000
Whitney Hodges: Right now, um, as well as like dollar a day retargeting ads, which you're doing also, but the additional layer that we recommend having in there is what we call client attraction ads that are running to completely cold audiences.

00:17:01.000 --> 00:17:21.000
Whitney Hodges: And those are low budget as well, like usually just a couple of dollars a day there, but like video views campaigns that are, you know, specifically targeting people that we know haven't seen you before. They haven't visited the website before. They haven't seen you on social media before. So that helps get brand new eyes on the business every day in a really cost effective manner.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:40.000
Whitney Hodges: And then those people that have seen those top of funnel ads can be like followed up with, with the conversion ads, with the retargeting ads as well. And so what we also do inside of the ads accelerators is really kind of break down what makes great content, what makes great.

00:17:40.000 --> 00:17:56.000
Whitney Hodges: add creatives, and add copy for each stage, um, of the… of the funnel, right? And we include lots of great examples in there for you, um, but we also give you personalized feedback, if you'd like it, um, as well, to where you can, you know.

00:17:56.000 --> 00:18:12.000
Whitney Hodges: Submit ads to us for review, submit your landing page to us for review, for example. Um, submit email and nurture text sequences to us, you know, for review as well, so that you can kind of get our expert eyes on it. Um, and we can point out opportunities that.

00:18:12.000 --> 00:18:27.000
Whitney Hodges: Um, sometimes when you're in the business, right, you're, you know, it makes it hard to, to be able to see what could be better or what's, what's going wrong. Um, but for us who are seeing it in so many, you know, businesses across the US that specialize in the wedding industry.

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:36.000
Whitney Hodges: um, we're able to kind of spot those areas of opportunity. And sometimes the smallest tweaks can make a really big difference in terms of results.

